<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's J.Martins no comment on Vidago.</title>
<headline>Portugal's J.Martins no comment on Vidago.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese retailing group Jeronimo Martins &amp; Filho-SGPS declined to comment on Wednesday on a media report that it was buying mineral water concern Vidago, Melgaco &amp; Pedras Salgadas.</p>
<p>&quot;There is nothing to say on the subject,&quot; a spokesman said when asked to comment by Reuters.</p>
<p>TSF radio reported that businessman Jose Sousa Cintra, who controls Vidago, had sold his stake to Jeronimo Martins.</p>
<p>Vidago shares were suspended on Tuesday by the Financial Markets Committee (CMVM).</p>
<p>--Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
